From 4971dd3dbaf214ee61c03005287126253a4a350a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:55:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux receiver: decode HEVC and offer it in hello.videoCaps

The receiver took every stream for H.264, so senders capped it at the
H.264 ceiling (4096x2304). Take the codec from streamConfig (PROTOCOL.md
6.5), parse HEVC access units, build the pipeline with h265parse and an
HEVC decoder, and offer HEVC up to the panel size when one is installed.
--no-hevc turns the offer off.
